<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#cataphract">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cataphract</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as cataphracts</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A cataphract was a heavily armoured cavalryman, with both rider and horse protected by armour, who charged with a long lance. Cataphracts were a principal component of the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a>, alongside highly mobile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horse-archer">horse archers</a>. The combination proved highly effective against Roman legions.</p></div>
